Article56

(1) In order to ensure the effectiveness of the implementation of the KLA policy in the Regency, a KLA Task Force is established.

(2) The establishment and membership composition of the KLA Task Force shall be determined by Regent's Decree.

(3) The KLA Task Force is domiciled at the Office of the Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Agency. (4) The KLA Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1) has the main tasks:

a. coordinating the implementation of policies and development of KLA;
b. conducting socialization, advocacy and communication of information and education on KLA policies;

(31)

c. collecting basic data for KLA development; d. conducting needs analysis based on basic data;

e. disseminating basic data;

f. determining the focus and priority of programs in realizing KLA, which are adjusted to regional potential;

