Article 36

(1) The Regency Government in efforts to fulfill children's rights is responsible for:

a. establishing and implementing policies and programs/activities for fulfilling children's rights;
b. respecting and guaranteeing the human rights of every child without distinguishing ethnicity, religion, race, class, gender, ethnicity, culture and language, legal status of the child, birth order of the child, and physical and/or mental condition;

(23)

c. strengthening and developing institutions providing family quality improvement services in realizing children's rights; d. guaranteeing protection, care, and welfare of children while taking into account the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, or other persons legally responsible for the child;

e. providing facilities and infrastructure in the implementation of fulfillment of children's rights;

f. guaranteeing the right of children to express opinions in accordance with the age and intelligence level of the child;

g. conducting supervision and guidance in the framework of implementation; and

h. conducting cooperation with private parties and/or Non-Governmental Organizations in the implementation of Protection of children.

(2) The responsibility of the Regency Government in efforts to protect children as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by regional apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.

Article 10

(1) The Regency Government in efforts to Protect women is responsible for:

a. establishing and implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women;
b. making efforts to prevent acts of Violence against women including criminal acts of trafficking in persons;
c. improving the effectiveness of services for women victims of acts of Violence;
d. improving efforts to protect female workers;
e. strengthening and developing institutions providing women's protection services;
f. cooperating with the Government, other Regional Governments, the private sector, the business community and/or Non-Governmental Organizations in efforts to prevent acts of Violence against women;
g. involving the active role of families, customary leaders, religious leaders, communities, and institutions in the field of women's protection.

(12)

(2) The responsibility of the Regency Government in efforts to protect women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by regional apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions and may coordinate with relevant agencies.

Article 81

(1) In order to prevent violations of women's rights, the community:

a. supervises various conditions occurring in their environment that may cause violations of women's rights;
b. increases awareness of violations of women's rights;
c. strengthens the role of community organizations, religious organizations and the family environment;
d. conducts supervision of the implementation of Women and Child Protection organized by the Regional Government through a mechanism of conveying aspirations to the Regent or Regional People's Representative Council.

(39)

(2) In order to prevent violations of children's rights, the community:

a. supervises various conditions occurring in their environment that cause violations of children's rights;
b. increases awareness of violations of children's rights;
c. strengthens the role of community organizations, religious organizations and the family environment; and
d. prevents early marriage.

Article 5

( 1) In order to improve the quality of life of women, the regional government is responsible for:

a. respecting and guaranteeing the rights of women without discrimination in accordance with human dignity;
b. implementing Gender Mainstreaming in the Regency; c. establishing a Gender Mainstreaming working group in the Region; d. improving Women's Empowerment in terms of role, quality and capacity in the fields of (9)
1. politics;
2. law;
3. social;
4. economy; and
5. culture.
e. strengthening and developing institutions providing Women's Empowerment services in the Regency.
(2) The responsibility of the Regency Government in efforts to improve the quality of life of women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by regional apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.

